&#8220;Karasu&#8221;

Ae! group&#8217;s &#8220;Dekoboko Life&#8221; follows at No. 2. The theme song for the film Osomatsusan The Movie first dropped digitally on May 11 to debut at No. 6 on the tally, and returns this week at No. 2 following the CD release on June 17. M!LK&#8217;s &#8220;Bakuretsu Aishiteru&#8221; climbs to No. 3 from No. 6 the week before, as the group places five titles in the top 50 simultaneously: &#8220;Bakuretsu Aishiteru&#8221; (No. 3), &#8220;Sukisugite Metsu!&#8221; (No. 5), &#8220;Idol Power&#8221; (No. 16), &#8220;Shin Unmei (Shunta Sono & Jutaro Yamanaka)&#8221; (No. 17), and &#8220;Iijan&#8221; (No. 43). CUTIE STREET&#8217;s &#8220;CUTIE SPHERE&#8221; also makes a significant move, vaulting 39-7.

Meanwhile, Michael Jackson&#8217;s biopic is powering his catalog up the Japan Hot 100: &#8220;Beat It&#8221; rises 50-32, &#8220;Billie Jean&#8221; 61-37, while &#8220;Thriller&#8221; and &#8220;Bad&#8221; re-enter at No. 84 and No. 96, respectively — bringing the late King of Pop’s simultaneous entries to four this week. Meanwhile, Arashi places 13 titles within the top 100, the group’s catalog continuing to hold steady across the chart although down from 19 last week.

The Billboard Japan Hot 100 combines physical and digital sales, audio streams, radio airplay, video views and karaoke data.

